  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts were correct; no parts added or dropped.",
   "Parts list says 3 x 100 ohm resistors; the schematic label says 10k. The parts list text is followed (value=100).",
   "Speaker red lead goes to port 1 and black lead to port 2 (the speaker is non-polarised). Black leads go to the top negative rail (tn), which the black jumper links to Uno GND.",
   "The image labels the top half rows f-j and the bottom half a-e. The catalogue naming is used instead: top half is bank t with rows a-e, bottom half is bank b with rows f-j.",
   "Each resistor spans the centre gap in its column (8, 17 and 25). Its top end shares a strip with the speaker's red lead. Its bottom end shares a strip with the coloured signal wire.",
   "Rail hole numbers (tn.1, tn.9, tn.17, tn.25) are approximate. The whole rail is one strip, so the exact hole does not matter electrically.",
   "Speaker pins: pin 8 goes to the speaker in column 8, pin 7 to column 17 and pin 6 to column 25, as in the schematic and the image."
  ]
 },
